Reactome metabolism genes (R-HSA-1430728, release 97) were downloaded from \url{https://reactome.org}. The gene list contains 2,197 genes and was verified with SHA-256 hash \texttt{1e7f5adf240a04c95cb30fd2a8ef83bcab7d519f5f2d12447d8b3112b9589164}. After intersecting with the expression matrix, 1,984 metabolic genes were retained.

\subsection{Normalization and Preprocessing}
Raw UMI counts were normalized per cell by dividing by the library size and multiplying by 10,000, then log-transformed using the log1p function:
\begin{equation}
    x'_{ig} = \log\left(1 + \frac{10,000 \cdot x_{ig}}{\sum_g x_{ig}}\right)
\end{equation}
where $i$ indexes cells, $g$ indexes genes, $x_{ig}$ is the raw UMI count, and $x'_{ig}$ is the normalized expression. Features with $<500$ counts in $<20\%$ of cells were filtered out.

